<!-- question: 169576 -->
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>MAT322 - Adaptive Quadrature Error</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>In Adaptive Quadrature using Simpson's Rule, suppose we have:</p>
<ul>
<li>\(S(a,b) = {@S1@}\) (approximation on the whole interval)</li>
<li>\(S(a, \frac{a+b}{2}) + S(\frac{a+b}{2}, b) = {@S2@}\) (sum of approximations on two halves)</li>
</ul>
<p>Estimate the magnitude of the error in the more accurate approximation \({@S2@}\).</p>
<p>Error \(\approx\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>The error estimate for Adaptive Simpson's Quadrature is given by:</p>
<p>\[ |E| \approx \frac{1}{15} |S_2 - S_1| \]</p>
<p>where \(S_1 = S(a,b)\) and \(S_2 = S(a, \frac{a+b}{2}) + S(\frac{a+b}{2}, b)\).</p>
<p>\[ |E| \approx \frac{1}{15} |{@S2@} - {@S1@}| = \frac{1}{15} ({@abs(S2-S1)@}) = {@ta1@} \]</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber></idnumber>
