  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>MAT322 - Degree of Precision</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>What is the degree of precision of {@rule_name@}?</p>
<p>Degree = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>The degree of precision of a quadrature formula is the largest integer \(n\) such that the formula is exact for all polynomials of degree at most \(n\).</p>
<ul>
<li>Trapezoidal Rule: Exact for linear functions (degree 1), but not quadratics. Degree = 1.</li>
<li>Simpson's Rule: Exact for cubic functions (degree 3), but not quartics. Degree = 3.</li>
<li>Midpoint Rule: Exact for linear functions (degree 1). Degree = 1.</li>
</ul>
<p>For {@rule_name@}, the degree of precision is {@ta1@}.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
