  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>MAT322 - Error Scaling</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>The error term for the Composite {@rule_name@} is \(O(h^{@power@})\).</p>
<p>If the step size \(h\) is halved (divided by 2), by what factor is the error approximately reduced?</p>
<p>Factor = [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked Solution</h3>
<p>Since the error is proportional to \(h^{@power@}\), if we replace \(h\) with \(h/2\), the new error is proportional to \((h/2)^{@power@} = \frac{h^{@power@}}{2^{@power@}}\).</p>
<p>The error is reduced by a factor of \(2^{@power@} = {@ta1@}\).</p>]]></text>
